{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>But.</b> As the Targum renders: בְּקוּשְׁטָא. And I saw in Bereshit Rabbah it is the language of Romaean — בְּרַם:" "<b>Has come upon us.</b> Its reason is the bet — because it is in the past tense, since it has already come; and its Targum is אֲתַת לָנָא."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {0 "Onkelos renders אבל as בקושטא, Aramaic for 'in truth / indeed.' Rashi cites a midrash identifying אבל as derived from the 'Romaean' (Greco-Roman) tongue, glossed by the Aramaic ברם, 'however / but.'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:03:14.673727906Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}